+ * A PS3 pad has no adaptive triggers; on a DualSense the triggers get a feel
+ * from what the title already does:
+ *   - the right trigger clicks like a gun's: resistance up to a break point,
+ *     then free travel. It reads as pressed only past the break (about half
+ *     way), so a shot goes off at the click;
+ *   - the left trigger has a light, even resistance (aiming);
+ *   - while the right trigger is held and the title runs the motors (a
+ *     weapon firing), the right trigger buzzes with them instead.
