+ * binds them to. They go out through SDL_GameControllerSendEffect as the
+ * trigger blocks of the DualSense output report (the layout SDL's
+ * testgamecontroller sends), only when they change; both triggers are set
+ * free again when the controller is closed and when the process exits. A
+ * controller that refuses the effect (not a DualSense, or no enhanced mode)
+ * keeps free triggers and the usual press point.
+ *
+ *   PS3_PAD_ADAPTIVE=0        off: free triggers, pressed past 3000 as before
+ *   PS3_PAD_FIRE_AT=<10-90>   where the right trigger reads as pressed, in
+ *                             percent of its travel (50)
